WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.994
A four-storey apartment block folds into a suitcase.

00:00:04.014 --> 00:00:06.579
The ground beneath it stays behind.

00:00:06.599 --> 00:00:12.950
FOOTPRINT is a complete English-language feature screenplay, intended to run fifty-five to sixty minutes.

00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:20.132
Ruth, a removal inspector, is selling her inherited engine yard to buy a coastal motel.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:24.375
She has already assigned her daughter, Lena, the front desk.

00:00:24.395 --> 00:00:28.765
Lena, a bus mechanic, has earned her own marine apprenticeship.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:35.721
Rushing her last job, Ruth signs a sixteen-flat building empty without walking inside.

00:00:35.741 --> 00:00:38.647
She folds it with thirty-two people still at home.

00:00:39.642 --> 00:00:42.204
Her yard gives them a safe way out.

00:00:42.224 --> 00:00:45.226
But their home needs somewhere permanent to stand.

00:00:45.246 --> 00:00:51.618
Marta, the cooperative chair, holds its original master plan—and the right to refuse another move.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.649
Trying to preserve her sale, Ruth gambles on a cramped site.

00:00:56.669 --> 00:01:00.124
The south wall cracks; a volunteer is hurt.

00:01:00.144 --> 00:01:05.194
Bell, the developer buying her yard, refuses to return the old site.

00:01:05.214 --> 00:01:09.014
He offers secure building storage and temporary beds.

00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:11.584
The residents accept and start packing.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.125
Each fold of the original paper changes the building.

00:01:16.145 --> 00:01:19.260
A moving crease can become a dangerous stairwell.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.346
A tear leaves a real crack.

00:01:21.366 --> 00:01:25.032
During the final unfolding, other hands control the plan.

00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:31.042
Ruth can still sell, hire a motel manager, and have the life she wants.

00:01:31.062 --> 00:01:35.082
She chooses to give the cooperative permanent title to her land.

00:01:35.102 --> 00:01:39.649
She keeps no flat, no authority, and no promise that Lena will stay.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:43.241
Lena leaves for her apprenticeship.

00:01:43.261 --> 00:01:45.798
The residents enter a home they chose.

00:01:45.818 --> 00:01:47.434
The wall stays crooked.

00:01:48.433 --> 00:01:54.722
The visual approach pairs tactile paper, worn concrete and restrained impossible movement.

00:01:54.742 --> 00:01:59.711
One building, one night, one family gives the feature a focused scale.

00:01:59.731 --> 00:02:03.097
A city of portable homes gives the world room to grow.
